  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nEscape Room Experience:\nOPERATION SPYCATCHER\n\nOnce in a while, the museum is transformed into an immersive ‘escape room’ experience in which you have the run of the main gallery after-hours, to follow themed clues and solve puzzles hidden within the museum.  Under the vigilant gaze of your experienced handler, you and the rest of your team, once briefed, become Special Operations Executive (S.O.E) agents, that have just landed by Horsa Glider - behind enemy lines…\n\nYour mission?  Solve the puzzles and crack the clues to find a missing list of suspected double agents and reveal the identity of the duplicitous spy.  This information must be placed into the hands of a senior member of the War Office within the 45 minutes, otherwise it will fall into enemy hands and put the mission to end the war at risk!\n\nHOSTED BY...\n\nHosted by experienced team-building facilitator and crime fiction author Helen Saxton of Dead Herring, as your handler, keeping the energy pacy, you are sure to have a memorable and inspirational evening for your teams in the museum!\n\nThe whole experience takes up to 90 minutes, including snacks and drinks, briefing, 45-minute puzzle-solving activity, debriefing and congratulations with ‘photo-booth’.\n\nTHE PUZZLES\n\nOnce you've received your video briefing on board a full size replica section of a horsa glider, you have to find the clues leading to eight different hands-on puzzles, hidden around the museum and corresponding to stories and themes in the museum.  Each one you solve reveals a clue to the next to the ultimate aim of decoding the name of the double agent.  Only with this vital intelligence can you escape the museum and deliver your findings to the War Office for your congratulations!\n\nRATES\n\n£45.00 per person with a minimum group booking requirement.\n\nIncludes one glass of house wine/ fruit juice per person, hot served canapes and a congratulatory group photo opportunity in the trench or shelter.\n\nEXAMPLE TIMINGS\n\nAn Escape Room Night can host three sessions of up to 10 people each.  Please contact us to discuss your needs. An example of timings is below.\n\n5:45pm – 7:15pm\nArrival & Refreshments - From 5.45pm\nEscape Room Experience: 6.15pm - 7.00pm\n\n7:00pm – 8:30pm\n\nArrival & Refreshments - From 7.00pm\nEscape Room Experience: 7.30pm - 8.15pm\n\n8:15pm- 9:45pm\n\nArrival & Refreshments - From 8:15pm\nEscape Room Experience: 8:45pm – 9:30pm\n\nSCHEDULING\n\nThe next Escape Room Night is running on 15th May (check the calendar to book a time slot).  For a scheduled night there is a minimum booking charge of 6 persons for a time slot.\n\nIf you would like to request a particular date for your group or company, please get in touch via the booking form to discuss your needs and the minimum required to run it.\n\nDo you and your comrades have what it takes to escape the museum? Enquire using the contact form below to book.\n\nYour Name\nYour Email\nHow many people are in your group?\nWhat date(s) were you interested in booking?\nMessage\nContact Us\nEscape Room – Against the Clock\n\nEscape Room – The clock is ticking\n\nEscape Room – Secret rendezvous\n\nEscape Room – Find a way out\n\nEscape Room – Tools of the trade\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
